I always look at my calendar on the mobile phone.
At eleven o'clock on Saturday, I have a problem.
I make a phone call to the hair salon again.
A woman answers.
"Namaste, I am Maya speaking," I say.
"Namaste Maya madam," she says.
"My haircut time is at eleven o'clock on Saturday," I say.
"But at eleven o'clock I have another plan."
"I want a time change."
"What time is suitable?" she asks.
"Is there time in the afternoon at half past two?" I ask.
She checks.
"Yes, on Saturday afternoon at half past two there is time," she says.
"Excellent, please fix half past two," I say.
"Yes madam, now the time is at half past two," she says.
"Thank you," I say.
I finish the phone call.
Now everything is in order.
I am happy.
